Mint_CompanySafeMinter_Unit_Concrete_Test
├── when the minter is called directly and not by delegatecall
│   └── it should revert with NotDelegateCall
├── when the namespace is empty
│   └── it should revert with EmptyNamespace
├── when the company is empty
│   └── it should revert with EmptyCompany
├── when the founder's Safe is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with InvalidFounderSafe
├── when the founder's Safe is the owners sentinel
│   └── it should revert with InvalidFounderSafe
├── when the founder's Safe is Companies House
│   └── it should revert with InvalidFounderSafe
├── when the founder's Safe has no code
│   └── it should revert with InvalidFounderSafe
├── when the factory deploys at another address than the derived one
│   └── it should revert with DerivedAddressMismatch
├── given the derived Safe has no code
│   ├── it should deploy it through the Safe proxy factory with the Safe L2 singleton and no module and the namespace and company and founder salt
│   ├── it should swap Companies House for the founder's Safe through a v 1 approved signature
│   ├── it should emit CompanySafeMinted with deployed true
│   ├── it should write no storage of Companies House
│   └── it should return the Safe
├── given the derived Safe is already deployed
│   ├── it should deploy nothing
│   ├── it should swap Companies House for the founder's Safe
│   └── it should emit CompanySafeMinted with deployed false
├── given the Safe was already minted
│   └── it should revert because Companies House is no longer an owner
└── when the Safe refuses the swap without reverting
    └── it should revert with SwapRefused
